Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: aot_cost.py measures what a recompiled game costs
 in disk and time, on generated code and on a cache (#18)

measure: generated C compiled for AArch64, lifted by Remill and compiled in six variants (no unwind tables, slim
objects, -Os, -O1, thin LTO, 64 functions per object), with the size and the sections of the objects, the CPU time,
the compressed sizes and the link. cache-stats: read-only, the files and sizes of an AOT cache folder and, for a
random sample of its objects, their sections and compression. No behaviour of the build changes: this only measures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: A tool that measures the disk and time cost of a recompiled game, so that the choice of how to lower it rests on numbers
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#18

